SUMMARY:Jimmy Dewrance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T203000
UID:2606177asyaV0vsU-DrqIX02fiAQ
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for a night of West Coast blues with grit\, soul\, a
 nd a rocking edge as Jimmy Dewrance comes to the Empress Marquee Club.\n\n
 Jimmy is a San Jose blues veteran\, harmonica player\, singer\, songwriter
 \, and bandleader with decades of old-school blues behind him. His sound h
 as been described as straight-up blues with a rocking chaser: harmonica up
  front\, dirty guitar\, solid bass\, and a heavy shuffle backbeat that get
 s the room moving.\n\nFans of Paul Butterfield\, John Mayall\, Freddie Kin
 g\, Albert King\, and B.B. King will feel right at home. Expect blues harp
 \, soulful vocals\, rock\, funk\, and a deep groove made for a live room.\
 n\nThe Marquee Club is the right setting for this kind of show: close\, wa
 rm\, and built for music you can feel. Come early for dinner\, grab a drin
 k\, and settle in for a Thursday night of real blues energy.\n\nDoors open
  for dinner at 5:30 p.m. Music at 6:30 p.m.
LOCATION:Empress Marquee Club
URL:https://empresstheatre.org/event/jimmy-dewrance/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jan Gross: Between The Veils: Featured June Artist
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T170000
UID:260615t6otvDNwbE-ZgRTPeI_1MA
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center is proud to present t
 he work of Jan Gross in the West Room of the Maurice Del Mue Galleries in 
 June.  There will be a reception for the artist on June 14th from 4-7 pm.
  \n\n Woodacre artist Jan Gross developed an early connection to the nat
 ural world from her early years in Ontario\, Canada with countless hours s
 pent exploring woods and waterways\, experiences that continue to inform h
 er art. A lifelong painter\, landscape designer\, and dedicated meditation
  practitioner\, she draws inspiration from the dynamic interplay of earth\
 , air\, water\, and fire\, often working in the liminal spaces where one e
 lement meets another. ***Between the Veils*** explores love\, loss\, mem
 ory\, and transformation through the language of the body. Rich with lumin
 ous color and emotional depth\, Her work reflects her belief in painting a
 s both a spiritual practice and a path toward healing.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/jan-gros
 s-june-featured-artist-in-the-del-mue-galleries
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eva Thomas: June Featured Artist in the Maurice Del Mue Galleries
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T170000
UID:260615ks9N5YBEq06jlTwqbezXlw
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center is proud to present t
 he art of Eva Thomas in the Maurice Del Mue Galleries in June.  There wil
 l be a reception for the artist on Sunday\, June 14th from 4-7PM.\n\nEva T
 homas is a West Marin based artist studying studio art at San Francisco St
 ate University. She works primarily with ink\, acrylic and spray paint. He
 r art is inspired by the human experience and connection to the natural el
 ements. Eva's work often includes images of faces\, bodies\, and elements 
 from nature. Her goal within her art practice is to connect with the other
 s and make sense of the ever-changing social landscape in which we live. H
 er current work has been focusing on sculptural and multimodal art forms\,
  encapsulating and documenting aspects of her experiences\, observations\,
  and mindsets in college.
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/eva-thom
 as-june-featured-artist-in-the-del-mue-galleries
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NOAH GALUTEN
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T180000
UID:260614583Wkao8F0CGh27U8r6JHw
DESCRIPTION:HEALDSBURG --\n\nWe're excited to welcome chef\, food writer\,
  and James Beard Award-winning cookbook author Noah Galuten to The Burrow 
 in Healdsburg in celebration of his new cookbook\, *Grill Time!: Why You 
 Should Be Grilling for Better\, Healthier\, Easier\, and More Delicious Me
 als*.\n\nJoin Noah and Chef David Baeli for an afternoon of live grilling\
 , cookbook-inspired fare\, and excellent local wine. Guests may purchase a
  mixed grilled plate featuring recipes from *Grill Time!*\, with wines av
 ailable from Right Turn Wine Co.\n\nPurchase a copy of the book at the eve
 nt and receive a special discount on your meal.\n\nReservations are recomm
 ended - https://www.opentable.com/r/the-burrow-healdsburg\n\nWhether you'r
 e a seasoned grill master or simply looking for fresh inspiration for summ
 er cooking\, this is a flavorful opportunity to spend an afternoon with on
 e of today's most engaging voices in food.\n\n**Thursday\, June 18 | 12:00
 –6:00 PM**\n\nThis is a free event. No registration required.\n\n**Your 
 new go-to grilling guide\, perfect for newbies and grill masters alike\, f
 rom the James Beard Award–winning writer and chef and author of *The Do
 n’t Panic Pantry Cookbook***\n\n***“Grill Time!* is Noah Galuten’s 
 love letter to the magic of live fire—how it makes weeknight cooking eas
 ier\, weekend cooking more fun\, and family meals more joyful. With clear 
 techniques and bold\, flexible recipes\, this is grilling built for real l
 ife.” —J. Kenji Lopez-Alt\, author of *The Wok* and *The Food Lab***
 \n\nIn Noah Galuten’s backyard\, it’s always grill time! With two youn
 g children\, Galuten knows firsthand how important it is to get flavorful\
 , healthy food on the table quickly and easily. His secret: the grill\, wh
 ich allows easily customizable dinners for all different palates. In Grill
  Time! Galuten embraces his love of bright flavors\, comfort foods\, and v
 eggie-forward dishes to create meals that work for backyard barbecues\, po
 ol parties\, camping trips\, and\, of course\, quick weeknight dinners.\n\
 nHere are delicious options for meat eaters\, vegetarians\, and vegans ali
 ke:\n\n\\*THE BEST BURGERS AND SANDWCHES! From Backyard Bacon Cheeseburger
 s\, the Juiciest Turkey Burgers\, and Pork Souvlaki Pitas to a Tofu Bánh 
 Mì with Lemongrass BBQ Sauce and a Smoky Grilled Caprese Sandwich\, there
 ’s something for everyone.\n\n\\*VEGGIE SIDES AND MAINS GALORE: Grilled 
 Asparagus and Wilted White Cheddar\, Perfect Grilled Potatoes\, Miso-Butte
 r Corn\, Stuffed Poblanos with Cilantro-Lime Tahini\, a Grilled Veggie Bur
 rito like no other\, and so much more.\n\n\\*BIG SALADS! A Southwest Veggi
 e Chop\, a Spicy Grilled Chicken Caesar with Garlic Bread Croutons\, and a
  Grilled Shrimp Niçoise\, to name just a few.\n\n\\*FISH AND SEAFOOD: Fro
 m Grilled Clams with Cocktail Butter to Grilled Fish Tacos with Chile Crun
 ch and Smoke-Grilled Miso Black Cod.\n\n\\*CHICKEN\, BEEF\, AND PORK\, eve
 ry which way: Achiote-Lime Chicken Breast and Pickle-Brined Drumsticks wit
 h Spicy Honey\; a Taverna Steak for weeknights and a Smoke-Grilled Bone-In
  Rib Eye for weekends\; a Buttermilk-Brined Pork Chop with Grilled Lemon a
 nd Smoke-Grilled Baby Backs.\n\nThere’s also a special guide to the ulti
 mate Hermosillo-Style Carne Asada. And for any newbies on the grill\, or p
 ros who want to expand their grill knowledge\, *Grill Time!* is a helpfu
 l guide on grill mechanics\, including the differences between smokers\, g
 as grills\, and charcoal grills and the cooking techniques that go along w
 ith each one. Level up your grilling game with *Grill Time!*\n\n**Author: 
 Noah Galuten** is a chef\, James Beard Award-winning cookbook author and a
 uthor of *The Don’t Panic Pantry Cookbook*. He is also the co-author of
  *On Vegetables: Modern Recipes for the Home Kitchen* with Jeremy Fox\, 
 and *Bludso's BBQ Cookbook: A Family Affair in Smoke and Soul* with Kevin
  Bludso\, among other titles. He currently lives in Los Angeles with his w
 ife\, children and small dog.
LOCATION:The Burrow
URL:https://copperfieldsbooks.com/event/2026-06-18/noah-galuten
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
