BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma AI - Agents & Tiny AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260619T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260619T190000
UID:260617RABOAgaAxEaFAzapEFJHFQ
DESCRIPTION:This is an in-person event! Registration is required in order 
 to get the address and get in.\n\n​Topic: Sonoma AI Meetups for remote 
 tech workers\, to build a North Bay AI community\, collaboratively learn\,
  share ideas\, and network with others who are building the future of AI.\
 n\n​What we’ll do: Meet & learn about AI tools\, AI infrastructure\, a
 nd AI best practices - with food \\+ wine.\n\n​Tech Talk 1: Your AI Pai
 r Programmer Hates Your Tech Debt Too Speaker: Shagun Bhatia\, Atlassian A
 bstract: Tech debt is a problem every engineering team knows is real\, but
  rarely has the time or clarity to tackle systematically. It compounds sil
 ently - slowing down feature work\, increasing bug rates\, and making onbo
 arding painful - until it's too expensive to ignore. In this talk\, I'll w
 alk through how we built an AI-assisted tech debt workflow at Atlassian th
 at goes far beyond static analysis.\n\n​Tech Talk 2: It's Not the Model
 . It's What You Fed It. Speaker: Zayne Turner\, Workato Abstract: When you
 r AI agent fails\, the instinct is to blame the model: try a different one
 \, adjust the prompt\, add more context. But most agent failures aren't mo
 del problems. They're design problems. This talk looks at what happens ins
 ide an agent at runtime\, why naive tool design compounds failure\, and th
 ree principles for improving agent performance — drawn from an open-sour
 ce hotel operations system built to demonstrate the patterns at production
  scale.\n\n​Tech Talk 3: AI Wants to Be Local: Beating the Cloud on 30M
 B of RAM Speaker: Pete Warden\, Moonshine AI Abstract: Today many people a
 ssume that cutting-edge AI requires massive data centers. But if you’ve 
 ever used a voice interface that takes two full seconds to respond\, you k
 now the cloud is failing the user experience. In this talk\, you’ll lear
 n how rethinking transformer architectures with variable input windows and
  incremental streaming cache can drop latency to near-instantaneous levels
  and shrink RAM footprints down to less than 30MB. Discover why the future
  of AI isn't in the cloud\, but right on your device\, completely private 
 and offline.\n\n​Who Should attend: Anyone interested in talking and lea
 rning about developing Agentic AI Apps.\n\n​Where: This is an in-person 
 event. Registration is required to get the address and into the event. Reg
 istration in advance will close 2 days before the event.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Library
URL:https://luma.com/jz1s0dbj
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
