BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cruzando la Montaña de Sonoma - A Hike in Spanish
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T143000
UID:260610gXxBImZZ00ayEE5J8BrQ7A
DESCRIPTION:El Parque Histórico Estatal Jack London presenta "Rutas y Ave
 nturas"\, una serie de caminatas gratuitas en español.\n\nEl sábado 20 d
 e junio\, únase a una caminata inolvidable —guiada en español— que c
 onecta el Parque Histórico Estatal Jack London con el hermoso Parque Regi
 onal North Sonoma Mountain. La participación y la entrada al parque son t
 otalmente gratuitas \\(se requiere inscripción previa\\).\n\nEsta caminat
 a exigente\, de 8\,5 millas \\(aprox. 13\,7 km\\) de recorrido\, ofrecerá
  las mejores vistas del valle\, rodeado de secuoyas y robles. Se ofrecerá
 n refrigerios y tentempiés para mantener al grupo con energía.\n\nLlegue
  a las 8:45 a. m. para registrarse\, de modo que el grupo pueda salir punt
 ualmente a las 9:00 a. m. La caminata finalizará aproximadamente a las 2:
 30 p. m. Lleve suficiente agua\, así como ropa y calzado cómodos y adecu
 ados para el clima y la actividad. Se recomienda el uso de bastones de sen
 derismo.\n\nSi tiene preguntas o necesita transporte\, comuníquese con Ca
 rlos Barragán al \\(707\\) 938-5216\, extensión 109\, o por correo elect
 rónico a cbarragan@jacklondonpark.com. Hay una cantidad limitada de mochi
 las y bastones de senderismo disponibles para préstamo.\n\nEs necesario i
 nscribirse con antelación. Por favor\, regístrese en https://jacklondonp
 ark.com/events/cruzando-sonoma/.\n\nJack London State Historic Park presen
 ts Rutas y Aventuras\, a series of free hikes in Spanish.\n\nOn Saturday\,
  June 20\, join an unforgettable trek – led in Spanish - connecting Jack
  London State Historic Park with the beautiful North Sonoma Mountain Regio
 nal Park.  Participation and park entry are completely free \\(registrati
 on is required\\).\n\nThis challenging \\(difícil\\) 8.5 miles hike will 
 include the best views of the valley\, surrounded by redwoods and oaks.  
 Snacks and refreshments will be provided to keep the group energized.\n\nA
 rrive at 8:45 a.m. for registration so the group can depart promptly at 9:
 00 a.m. The hike will end at approximately 2:30 pm.  Bring plenty of wate
 r\, comfortable clothing and footwear suitable for the weather and the act
 ivity. Hiking poles are recommended.\n\nIf you have questions or need tran
 sportation\, please contact Carlos Barragán at \\(707\\) 938-5216 ext. 10
 9 or via email at cbarragan@jacklondonpark.com.  A limited number of back
 packs and hiking pole are available to borrow.\n\nAdvance registration is 
 required.  Please register at https://jacklondonpark.com/events/cruzando-
 sonoma/.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/cruzando-sonoma/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Sonoma County Genealogical Society's Seminar
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T160000
UID:260610dtU-04_RtkKfP3FNUzQcEA
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma County Genealogical Society Seminar\n\n With Lisa 
 Gorrell and Cindy Brennan\n\nHow to Develop a Research Plan with Lisa Gorr
 ell\n\nFinding your Railroad Ties with Cindy Brennan\n\n Saturday\, June 
 20th\n\n FREE\n\n 1:00pm—4:00pm PDT\n\n Virtual via Zoom login beginn
 ing at 12:30 p.m.\n\nIn person come by noon and enjoy some light refreshme
 nts\n\n 1:00-2:00 How to Develop a Research Plan with Lisa Gorrell\n\n Do
  you feel like your research results go in circles\, that you keep finding
  the same information\, or you have brick walls you cannot solve? Lisa wil
 l explain how to create and use a research plan which will keep you focuse
 d on your research.\n\n Lisa S. Gorrell is a Certified Genealogist and ha
 s served on boards of several genealogical societies including the Sonoma 
 County Genealogical Society.\n\n 2:00-2:30 Interactive Break\n\n 2:30-3:
 30 Finding your Railroad Ties with Cindy Brennan\n\n There are only a few
  things that are as entwined with American history as the Railroad. For ma
 ny of our ancestors\, trains represented the most profound change in their
  lifetime. New careers\, travel\, food\, medicine and products that were n
 ever available before\, were now a possibility. Join us on a virtual train
  trip to learn how your family was connected to the magic of the Railroad.
 \n\n Cindy Brennan has been an avid family history researcher for over 20
  years. Since 2009\, she has served as the editor of the Sonoma County Gen
 ealogy Society's monthly newsletter.  \n\n This meeting is held in-pers
 on at the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints in the Cultural Hall
 \, 1725 Peterson Lane\, Santa Rosa or you can attend via Zoom.\n\n Even i
 f you are attending in person you must register at https://www.scgsonline.
 org\n\n Registration closes Friday\, June 19th
LOCATION:Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints
URL:https://www.scgsonline.org 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
