BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nature Wellness at Sonoma Garden Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T120000
UID:260612Eo7n7rgNXESKqQJFGPvT1w
DESCRIPTION:Join Sonoma Ecology Center and Sonoma County Ag \\+ Open Space
  for a gentle\, restorative Nature Wellness experience on June 20\, 10:00 
 am-12:00 pm at Sonoma Garden Park. This guided experience is inspired by t
 he Japanese practice of Shinrin Yoku\, which means “forest bathing.” F
 orest Bathing is the intentional practice of slowing down and immersing on
 eself in the sights\, sounds\, smells\, and sensations of the natural worl
 d in order to restore wellbeing and deepen our relationship with nature. W
 hile walking at a relaxed pace and seated in community\, a series of guide
 d invitations will awaken the senses and encourage personal connection to 
 the land. \n\nThe practice of Forest Therapy supports both personal and co
 llective healing. Certified Forest Therapy Guide Susan Karle brings over a
  decade of experience guiding nature connection practices with people of a
 ll ages\, and her approach integrates a background in grief and trauma wor
 k with a deep respect for the healing power of nature. \n\nThere is no cha
 rge for this outing\, which is made possible by the voters of Sonoma Count
 y who fund the work of Ag \\+ Open Space with a quarter-cent sales tax. \n
 \nChildren ages 8-11 must be accompanied by an adult.
LOCATION:Sonoma Garden Park
URL:https://www.farmtrails.org/event/saturday-harvest-market-at-sonoma-gar
 den-park-2/2026-06-20/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
