BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Cell Sundays: Callie Watts & Kris Dilbeck
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T143000
UID:260606EtIdaoJr_k2fvoje3SO4-Q
DESCRIPTION:**Callie Watts: Where Classic Sounds Meet Modern Soul**\n\nJoi
 n us for No Cell Sundays with Callie Watts\, a Northern California pop sin
 ger-songwriter whose sound is steeped in the golden era of songwriting.\n\
 nRaised on classical music\, The Beatles\, and The Beach Boys\, Callie dis
 covered her calling through the great writers of the '60s and '70s—Joni 
 Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy Joel\, and Caro
 le King. These legendary artists shaped her melodic writing style and cont
 inue to influence every note she plays.\n\nA versatile musician\, Callie h
 as spent her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, arranger\, and
  lead/backing vocalist—performing solo and with local and Bay Area bands
  across multiple genres. Expect an afternoon of soulful melodies\, timeles
 s classics\, and songs that transport you back to when music was everythin
 g.\n\n**What's No Cell Sundays?**\n\nIt's simple: disconnect from your dev
 ices\, reconnect with great wine\, live music\, and the people around you.
  *Check your phone with us at the door and receive a complimentary tasting
 .* Bring a blanket\, grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way it was m
 eant to be spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/no-cell-sundays-callie-watts
 -kris-dilbeck
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sister Act
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T153000
UID:260604NchK9Vn_PUmq0pdaVDicqQ
DESCRIPTION:**A Disco Diva\, a Choir in Crisis\, and a Whole Lot of Soul!*
 *\n\n***“One of the season’s happiest surprises.”* —Elisabeth Vinc
 entelli for New York Post**\n\n***Sister Act* is the high-energy musical c
 omedy based on the beloved 1992 film. Featuring an electrifying Alan Menke
 n score infused with disco and gospel beats\, this feel-good show is a cel
 ebration of music\, sisterhood\, and second chances.**\n\n**When disco div
 a Deloris Van Cartier witnesses a crime\, she’s forced into hiding—in 
 a convent! Disguised as a nun\, she transforms the struggling choir with h
 er powerhouse voice\, helping them find their sound while discovering her 
 own. Nominated for five Tony Awards\, *Sister Act* is a joyful\, soul-stir
 ring spectacle that proves music—and a little mischief—can work miracl
 es!**\n\nThursdays\, Fridays & Saturdays @ 7:30pm\, Saturdays and Sundays 
 at 2:00pm Run Time: Two hours\, 30 mins including intermission\n\nThursday
 s Adult $33Fri/Sat Eve Adult $44.95\; Senior $38.95\; Under 18 $31.95Sat/S
 un Matinee Adult $55.95\; Senior $48.95Value seating $37.95\\*All prices i
 nclude fees\n\n(707) 523-4185\n\n**boxoffice@6thstreetplayhouse.com**
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/sister-act/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Visiting Artist Tab Link\; Mid Range Soda Firing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T180000
UID:260602vXv-1HmGtEGYTECIyQDpKg
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday\, June 20: 9 AM – 5 PM\; Sunday\, June 
 21: 10 Am – 6 PM\; Tuesday\, June 23: 4 PM – 7 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 
 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nExperience Level\n\nIntermediate and Advanced\n\n
 Event Categories: Ceramics\, Workshops\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistrat
 ion\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$295\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal R
 egistration Cost:\n\n$295\n\nAbout the Class\n\nJoin Resident Alumni and V
 isiting Artist\, Tab Link as they teach the process of mid-range soda firi
 ng alongside our kiln facilitator\, Dan Clauson. Throughout the 3 day work
 shop\, students will receive an introduction to mid-range soda firing\, wi
 th hands-on training in the process of loading\, firing\, and maintaining 
 our crossdraft kiln named “Julia”. Participants in this workshop will 
 learn the fundamentals of atmospheric soda firing. The class will be instr
 ucted in the safety and care of the equipment as well as guided through th
 e firing process. This workshop includes instruction on glazing\, wadding 
 the ceramic pieces\, loading the kiln\, firing the kiln\, and kiln mainten
 ance\, with special instruction in Tab Link’s processes and firing techn
 iques.\n\nAn artist talk about their studio practice and history with firi
 ng\n\nPresentation on the History of Sodium based firing practices\n\nPres
 entation on the Basic Chemistry of Sodium Glazing\n\nPresentations will co
 ver information on both salt and soda firings\, their similarities/differe
 nces\, and shared histories. Participants will bring bisque-ware to be fir
 ed as bare clay or with slipped surfaces. There will be an assortment of f
 lashing slips and glazes to apply to the bisqueware on loading day for tho
 se who choose to use them. Each participant gets 1 cubic foot of firing sp
 ace.\\(Tip\; Make sure all your pots fit approximately into a milk crate w
 hich is 1 cubic foot of space\\).
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/tab-link-mid-range-soda-fir
 ing-workshop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
