DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T160000
UID:260511KD82DoetuEqo5UeOQMY5Ag
DESCRIPTION:Solstice in the Redwoods is a women's weekend retreat on the R
 ussian River\, designed for connection\, ritual\, and rest in a beautiful 
 natural setting. Spend your days in guided experiences like Tea &amp\; Tar
 ot\, a redwood walking meditation\, and river time with a cold plunge opti
 on\, along with space to unwind and integrate. The weekend culminates in a
  shared dinner and a Solstice fire ceremony under the stars. Hosted by the
  Magick Oak Collective.
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/solstice-in-the-redwoods?a
 ff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:S.R. Laws
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T000000
UID:260331aek1BNAAMk-nqWJe9S9uIw
DESCRIPTION:S.R. Laws: An inspiring Storyteller in Song\n\n        S.R. La
 ws is a performing and recording original musical artist whose work resona
 tes with a familiar warmth while introducing entirely fresh ideas. Hailed 
 by guitarist/promoter Scotty O’Neill as “an ORIGINAL songwriter who kn
 ows how to tell a story clearly in song\,” Laws has built a reputation f
 or songs that capture both nostalgia and innovation.\n\nEarly Influences a
 nd Musical Roots  \n\nGrowing up in Northern California\, Laws developed a
  deep bond with music at an early age. His father worked as a trash collec
 tor\, and young Scott Ray Laws \\(a.k.a. S.R. Laws\\) spent countless hour
 s digging through discarded 45-rpm records. Each discovery—whether caked
  in grime or found pristine—felt like unearthing treasure. The thrill of
  dropping the needle on something new ignited his lifelong passion for son
 g-craft.\n\nThe Texas Pilgrimage  \n\nWith only two suitcases and $500 to 
 his name\, Laws set out for Austin\, Texas—the “Live Music Capital of 
 the World.” There\, open‐mic nights and songwriter showcases became hi
 s classroom. Night after night\, he honed his craft\, forging connections 
 and absorbing the essence of Americana\, roots rock\, and modern folk.\n\n
  “It was such a treat catching your set last night—really refreshing t
 o hear something new and original. Thanks for pulling up a chair and hangi
 ng out with us—we really enjoyed the conversation and the stories behind
  your songs.” - Tripp B.\, Singer-Songwriter\n\nInfluences That Shaped H
 is Voice  \n\nLaws draws inspiration from master storytellers who paved th
 e way for heartfelt\, lyrical music. Artists who have left an indelible ma
 rk on his craft include:\n\n- John Hiatt  \n\n- Lucinda Williams  \n\n- Ro
 dney Crowell  \n\n- Neil Finn  \n\n- Patty Griffin  \n\n- Steve Earle  \n\
 n- Ron Sexsmith  \n\nTheir mastery of narrative and melody has shaped his 
 own artistic journey\, resulting in songs that feel both comfortingly fami
 liar and entirely “out there.”\n\nCritical Acclaim  \n\nColleagues and
  venue owners alike have praised his work and stage presence:  \n\n“Scot
 t Ray Laws is a unique and really cool songwriter…he digs into materials
 \, tells a story in his songs\, and has a clean baritone vocality that is 
 easy on the ears. We had a chance to meet and hang with Scott back in May
 …and I had to have him back for a Wednesday evening.” - Luigi\, Owner 
 of The Listening Room\n\n“Expect slow-burning passion and vivid music…
 the kind of energy that turns into ‘let’s stay for just one more!” -
  Doug\, Owner/Wine Maker at Spicy Vines\n\nCurrent Projects  \n\nNow based
  in Sonoma County\, California\, Laws works tirelessly as a recording\, wr
 iting & touring artist. Through over 100 gig dates a year\, intimate club 
 shows\, festival stages\, house concerts and late-night songwriter circles
 \, he invites audiences to join him on a musical journey—one heartfelt s
 tory at a time.\n\nWith a blend of classic influence\, modern vision\, and
  a voice that feels like home\, S.R. Laws continues to carve out his place
  in the American songwriting landscape.
LOCATION:Bloom Carneros
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108157631?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
