BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T193000
UID:260318y59UHv20ykG0HwibXf0b1A
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\nPre- requisite:\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach week\,
  we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connection 
 that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go beyond 
 the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate pat
 terns and styling\, including:\n\nTurns and Spins:\n\nMaster your inside a
 nd outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Toss moves.
 \n\nIntricate Patterns:\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, as well as va
 rious Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n\nFootwork a
 nd Styling:\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced footwork like t
 he Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work on styling with 
 a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.\n\nThis class i
 s your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead-follow connecti
 on\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your salsa vocabulary. 
 Join us and elevate your dance!\n\nDetails:\n\nNo partner necessary — ro
 tations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe so
 les to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get s
 ettled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 6:30PM – 7:30PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/intermediate-salsa-clas
 s/17159571/2026-06-23T18
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LEARN TO ROW **North Bay Rowing Club Summer Camp
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T120000
UID:2603099z-f23AyFEig2Bcw8k4DMA
DESCRIPTION:Learn-to-Row Summer Camp Information - North Bay Rowing Club\n
 \nAt the Learn-to-Row Summer Camp\, athletes will learn the fundamentals
  of the sport both on land and on the water. They will meet current member
 s of the team who will help guide and instruct them in proper form\, and l
 earn what it means to be a part of a team. Athletes will begin instruction
  on-land learning proper boat handling and basic sculling technique\, and 
 then they will practice their skills on-water in singles and team boats th
 at holds either 2 or 4 students in a shell. Students may have the opportun
 ity to learn more about racing skills and perform short distance races at 
 the end of the week-long session.\n\nSummer camps are open to all rowers
 \, whether you're a looking to explore a new sport or simply looking for a
  fun activity! No experience is required!\n\nAthletes: 13-17 years\n\nPrer
 equisite: No experience is required!!\n\nSession Days: Monday through Fri
 day\n\nSession Times : 9:00am -12:00pm\n\nLearn To Row Session Dates: Ses
 sion 1: June 22 - 26 Session 2: July 6 - 10 Session 3: July 13 - 17 Sessio
 n 4: July 20 - 24 Session 5: July 27 - 31
LOCATION:North Bay Rowing Club
URL:https://www.northbayrowing.org/2026-summer-camps/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
