BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Tools for Visual Artists
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T200000
UID:260618xjAETxL-T0iDVfdmQENlgQ
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13 and over\n\nAbout this Class:\n\nCurious about digital art but
  not sure where to begin? This hands-on workshop is designed for tradition
 al artists ready to expand their creative practice into the digital realm.
  You'll learn how to choose the right tools&mdash\;tablets\, apps\, and so
 ftware&mdash\;while exploring essential techniques like working with layer
 s\, brushes\, and digital color. The class also covers how to combine scan
 ned drawings with digital painting and prepare your artwork for high-quali
 ty prints. With a focus on experimentation and practical skills\, this wor
 kshop makes digital tools approachable\, intuitive\, and directly relevant
  to your existing artistic process.\n\nThis class is on ZOOM. You will rec
 eive a zoom link a few days before class.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nPryce 
 Jones is an artist\, designer\, and educator whose work explores how peopl
 e experience stories across digital\, physical\, and interactive environme
 nts. With a background in architecture\, video games\, and immersive media
 \, he began his career at Gensler before spending nearly two decades as an
  environment artist and art director with studios including LucasArts\, Ei
 dos\, Activision\, and Gazillion Entertainment. His current practice bridg
 es fine art\, creative placemaking\, and emerging technologies to engage c
 ommunities around history and identity. He has served as founding MFA Dire
 ctor at the Academy of Art University and now teaches Game Arts at the Cal
 ifornia College of the Arts\, mentoring the next generation of artists and
  designers.\n\nLearn more about Pryce: www.prycejonesart.com
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-digital-tools-z
 oom?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Art of What's Possible | Design + Construct an Accordion-style
  Book
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T120000
UID:260618Vw8QqodZzE2bSNEgZlDm8A
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 13\\+\n\nAn immersive\, hands-on visual art experience that will 
 spark curiosity\, creativity\, and a deep connection to the making process
 . By weaving in recycled and natural materials\, this workshop invites art
 ists to think sustainably while exploring inventive problem-solving and bo
 ld\, imaginative expression. Students will explore a variety of art materi
 als\, including acrylic paint\, pastels\, and found objects. Through paint
 ing and printmaking\, they will experiment with color\, texture\, and crea
 tive expression. Using their artwork\, students will then design and const
 ruct a unique accordion-style book\, incorporating interactive elements su
 ch as flaps and pockets.\n\nThis workshop is located in the classroom.\n\n
 About the Teacher: \n\nCristina Ruiz is a Mexican artist and educator with
  over 28 years of experience teaching students of all ages across diverse 
 cultural and community settings. Her work is deeply rooted in her cultural
  heritage\, often expressed through evocative soft sculptures that explore
  identity\, memory\, and storytelling through material and form. Throughou
 t her career\, she has fostered inclusive\, creative environments that hon
 or the richness of different traditions\, encouraging dialogue and connect
 ion through art. Cristina believes that the artistic process is as vital a
 s the final piece&mdash\;offering a space for exploration\, reflection\, a
 nd personal growth. By emphasizing process in art\, she supports learners 
 in developing confidence\, curiosity\, and a meaningful relationship with 
 their own creative voice.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-the-art-of-what
 s-possible?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:From Trash to Art: Dreamcatchers & Junk Journals
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T210000
UID:260618SoH1swVzzky0BeJ2FpgO0w
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 10\\+\n\nTransform everyday materials into meaningful\, one-of-a-
 kind creations in this playful\, hands-on workshop. Using a simple Trader 
 Joe's grocery bag as your base\, you'll craft a personalized junk journal&
 mdash\;perfect for sketching\, collaging\, or capturing ideas&mdash\;while
  exploring fun ways to cut\, layer\, and embellish. Then\, give new life t
 o forgotten items like old CDs and yarn as you learn to weave your own dre
 amcatcher. This class is all about creativity\, resourcefulness\, and seei
 ng beauty in the unexpected&mdash\;no experience needed\, just a willingne
 ss to experiment and have fun.\n\nThis workshop is located in the classroo
 m. \n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nAna Anzore is a lifelong artist and crafter 
 and longtime Petaluma resident. She has been the summer school and GATE pr
 ogram art teacher for three years for Waugh School District and has worked
  with children from grades 1-6. Ana has also had her own fun after school 
 art club where kids get to work with her private art supply collection.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-trash-to-art?a
 ff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Where Math Meets Imagination: The World of Algorithmic Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T150000
UID:260618H0kYeDfdh0a1Q__AaxcJ0w
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18 and over\n\nAbout this Class:\n\nThis engaging presentation ex
 plores the world of algorithmic art through the lens of Jeffrey Ventrella&
 mdash\;a pioneer in animated artificial life\, fractal geometry\, simulati
 on-based games\, and expressive virtual worlds. With advanced training in 
 both fine art and technology\, including graduate work at the MIT Media La
 b\, Ventrella translates complex ideas in math\, science\, and computation
  into accessible\, artist-friendly concepts. The talk features his work in
  fractal art and biologically inspired animation\, alongside a visual jour
 ney through the evolution of computer art from the 1970s to today. Drawing
  on his experience co-founding There.com and creating interactive experien
 ces in Second Life\, this presentation offers a rare\, inspiring look at t
 he intersection of art\, technology\, and digital culture.\n\nThis class i
 s located in the Main Gallery.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nJeffrey Ventrella
  began his artistic journey as a teenager\, exploring drawing\, painting\,
  and sculpture alongside a deep curiosity for geometry and biology. An ear
 ly fascination with computer-generated fractals led him to develop a disti
 nctive form of abstract art rooted in code. He holds degrees in Art Educat
 ion\, Art History\, and software-based Art and Design\, culminating in a M
 aster's degree from the MIT Media Lab. Throughout his career\, he has focu
 sed on design research within high-tech startups and university teaching\,
  specializing in virtual worlds\, game design\, and artificial life. Now\,
  he is dedicated to advancing his work in mathematical art and research.\n
 \nLearn more about Jeffrey: www.ventrella.com
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pacacademy-math-meets-imag
 ination?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alla Prima Essentials: Paint It in One Sitting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T160000
UID:260618G3PMrVTxbkSdCfYIQ88D5w
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nDive into the world of oils with this three-hour introdu
 ctory session designed specifically for those picking up a brush for the f
 irst time. We will strip away the intimidation of the medium by focusing o
 n the "alla prima"method\, where you'll learn to layer wet paint to create
  a finished still life in a single sitting. You'll get hands-on experience
  with essential kit basics\, from understanding brush shapes to the proper
  use of odorless mineral spirits and linseed oil. By focusing on seeing li
 ke an artist&mdash\;prioritizing big blocks of color and light over tiny d
 etails&mdash\;you will build the confidence to mix a full spectrum from a 
 limited palette and leave with a completed work of art.\n\nThis workshop i
 s located in the classroom.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nRachel Sager earned 
 her BFA in Painting from the Tyler School of Art after studying at Lorenzo
  de' Medici in Italy\, where she also worked as a portrait artist near the
  Duomo. Her work has been featured in international exhibitions including 
 Aqua Art Miami\, the Affordable Art Fair in New York City\, and the Crocke
 r-Kingsley California Biennial\, and she received first prize from Nancy L
 im in a Bay Area juried competition. She was also the featured artist and 
 narrator of the Emmy Award&ndash\;winning PBS documentary Sketching the Si
 lk Road. Now based in Northern California\, she runs Suite G Studio\, wher
 e she hosts figure drawing classes and curates exhibitions and performance
  events.\n\nLearn more about Rachel: \n\nwww.rachelsager.com@sagerpaint
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-alla-prima-pai
 nting?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Luminous Landscape: Mastering the "Wipeout" Underpainting and 
 Oil Glazing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260623T160000
UID:260610RUREzgN2E0GHMhGOPph-JA
DESCRIPTION:Buy an All Access Pass here. \n\nBuy a Lecture Pass here.\n\nF
 or Ages: 18\\+\n\nIn this workshop\, you move beyond simple shapes and exp
 lore how to infuse your work with mood and atmosphere. You will learn how 
 to build a composition from the ground up\, starting with a classic wipeou
 t technique to establish values before moving into the vibrant world of ac
 rylics.\n\nWhat You Will Learn:\n\nThe Foundation of Light: Master the "wi
 peout" method to create a roadmap for your painting. Color Mixing &amp\; H
 armony: Learn to blend pigments to create realistic skies\, rolling hills\
 , and textured foliage.The Painterly Approach: Move away from stiff lines 
 and embrace fluid\, expressive brushwork that breathes life into your canv
 as. Compositional Secrets: Understand how to guide the viewer's eye throug
 h a landscape using classic Hudson River School principles.This workshop i
 s located in the classroom.\n\nAbout the Teacher: \n\nNorthern California&
 ndash\;based artist Roberto Miliano creates atmospheric landscapes that br
 idge 19th-century tradition with contemporary vibrancy. Inspired by the To
 nalist and Hudson River School movements\, his work captures the mood of t
 he natural world&mdash\;from the foggy Pacific coast to quiet mountain wat
 ers. His process begins with intuitive sketching\, followed by acrylic und
 erpainting and layered oils that build rich\, dreamlike depth. Blending cl
 assical palettes with modern materials\, his paintings evoke both nostalgi
 a and a sense of quiet mystery.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/pac-academy-wipeout-oil-gl
 azing?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
