BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Amateur Radio Field Day: Radio\, Emergency Communications & Fox Hu
 nt
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T160000
UID:2606105Hn_sd7euU2Za_lU_mT3pw
DESCRIPTION:Join local amateur radio operators for ARRL Field Day at Silve
 r Oak Park in American Canyon. Field Day is a nationwide amateur radio eve
 nt where radio clubs set up temporary stations\, practice emergency commun
 ications\, and introduce the public to ham radio. This event is hosted by 
 the North Bay Amateur Radio Association.\n\nVisitors are welcome to stop b
 y\, see radio equipment in operation\, ask questions\, and learn how amate
 ur radio can help during emergencies when normal communication systems are
  overloaded or unavailable. We’ll also have beginner-friendly activities
 \, including a small “fox hunt” radio direction-finding demo where vis
 itors can try locating a hidden transmitter.\n\nNo radio license is requir
 ed to visit or participate in the public demonstrations. Families\, studen
 ts\, scouts\, emergency-preparedness volunteers\, and anyone curious about
  radio are welcome.
LOCATION:Silver Oak Park
URL:https://www.meetup.com/north-bay-amateur-radio-events/events/315151812
 /
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Estonian Folk Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T190000
UID:2606093L1PDuB4Q06NcM05XswLKg
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Estonian song and dance traditions the way it should
  be done - outside! Our own laulu- and tantsupidu takes place in Marin Cou
 nty\, at a location with a European village feel and gorgeous views.\n\nPa
 rticipating choirs include Noorus Segakoor\, members of the Rotalia Meesko
 or\, and singers from the West Coast cities and Baltimore-D.C.\, led by He
 ather MacLaughlin Garbes and Crista Berryessa. We’ll celebrate Jaanipäe
 v with cultural workshops\, games\, Midsummer Market\, activities for the 
 whole family\, and the company of friends.\n\nEvent schedule\n\n12 - 3 PM\
 n\nWest Coast dancers folk dance performance and workshop led by Liina Teo
 se\n\nChildren’s activities: visit with Kristi Roosmaa and workshop with
  young musicians\n\nMidsummer Market\, California wine tasting flights\, J
 aanipäev flower crown making\n\nSeminars on regilaul and workshop on rahv
 amängud with Kairi Leivo\n\nKannel studio with Inglikeeled\n\nSeminar wit
 h Bishop Sander\n\nFollowed By Catered Lunch\n\n4:30 PM\n\nThe festival’
 s featured song concert in two parts: combined choirs\, guest choirs and i
 nstrumentalists\n\nFollowed By Coffee and Dessert
LOCATION:Nativity of Christ Greek Orthodox Church
URL:https://www.lep2026.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Evening Programs at Bothe-Napa Valley State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T220000
UID:260608fvWvmycH2EuSzGDjJoQ9dQ
DESCRIPTION:Summer Evening Programs at Bothe-Napa Valley State Park are a 
 seasonal series of family-friendly evening events hosted by Napa Valley St
 ate Parks Association and Napa County Regional Park & Open Space District.
  Held throughout June and July\, the series features a rotating lineup of 
 programs including live music\, karaoke\, outdoor movies\, trivia\, and mo
 re. Bring a chair or blanket\, roast a s'more\, and enjoy a fun evening in
  the park!
LOCATION:Bothe-Napa Valley State Park 
URL:https://www.napavalleystateparks.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monthly Movement at The Village
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T100000
UID:260608IGnKwpNra0CSVSMEa6yz1w
DESCRIPTION:Start your morning with movement at Montgomery Village for our
  monthly fitness event. Join us for a class in partnership with lululemon 
 and Rise Cycle Co.\, designed to awaken your body and set the tone for the
  day ahead.\n\nThe class will take place on Saturday\, June 27th from 9:00
  to 9:45am at lululemon\, located at 2307 Magowan Drive. Our 45-min instru
 ctor-led strength training class combines weights\, bands\, body-weight ex
 ercises\, and cardio at a quicker pace to sculpt and tone your muscles! Cl
 asses are set to killer playlists\, driven by the beat of the music. Mats 
 and equipment will be provided\, so just show up and be ready to work! Scu
 lpt 45 is suitable for all fitness levels\, and the instructor is always h
 appy to provide modifications as needed.\n\nSpace is limited\, and advance
  registration is required. Attendees will be entered into a post-class raf
 fle for a chance to win a $100 Lululemon gift card\, Lululemon leggings\, 
 and a 5-class pack to Rise Cycle Co. Must be present to win.
LOCATION:Montgomery Village Lululemon
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/monthly-movement-at-the-village-
 2/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beyond Tea Cozies: Crochet Wrappings
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T160000
UID:260607qFnu38GrkkOBOU1a_IwiWg
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday · 1 Session\n\nDate & Time\n\nJune 27\, 
 2026\n\n1:00 PM – 4:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 201\, Fiber Arts Studio\n\
 nCategory\n\nFiber Arts\n\nExperience Level\n\nIntermediate\n\nAges\n\n13\
 \+\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$50\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nN/A\n\nTotal Registra
 tion Cost:\n\n$50\n\nprogram overview\n\nJoin us for an exploration of the
  innovative possibilities within crochet! This workshop invites you to del
 ve into the sculptural aspects of the craft by stitching directly onto nat
 ural objects and witnessing their transformation. Drawing inspiration from
  a rich tradition\, you will be introduced to a variety of techniques that
  help conform to the natural changes in shape\, accommodate extensions and
  tight corners\, leave open spaces\, and utilize essential materials such 
 as yarn\, crochet hook\, and natural items like twigs\, stones\, and shell
 s. Guided throughout the process\, you will engage with your materials\, i
 ntegrating them into form-fitting creations that breathe new life into fam
 iliar objects. These “cozies” not only redefine their purpose but also
  elevate them into unique artistic statements. By the end of the workshop\
 , you can expect to take home a few small finished pieces or work samples 
 to inspire further creativity. A basic understanding of crochet is require
 d. Please bring the following to the workshop:\n\nNatural objects to wrap:
  a stone \\(palm size\\)\, a shell 2-3 inches\, and a small branch section
 \, approx 6 inches length with 1-3 side branches. \n\nYarn: 2 skeins \\(d
 ifferent colors\\) of Pima 100 yarn.\n\nCrochet hook: Size 2.5 mm\n\nPleas
 e consider supporting Sonoma’s local yarn shop Noma Knits. Students rece
 ive a 10% discount when purchasing supplies for this workshop.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/beyond-tea-cozies-crochet-w
 rappings/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Botanical Blueprints: Introduction to Cyanotype
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T140000
UID:260607lQ0h4Tt4N0iCf4Y_k2ejPQ
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday\, June 27\, 2026 10:00 AM – 2:00 PM\n\n
 Location\n\nRoom 110\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nEvent Categories:
  Bilingual\, Drawing & Painting\, Fiber Arts\, Printmaking\, Workshops\n\n
 Age\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$90\n\nMaterials Fee:\
 n\n$10\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nLearn cyanotype photography 
 basics in this fun intro class. Expose botanical blueprints using sun and 
 light-sensitive chemicals\, then take home four 8×10 prints.\n\nAbout the
  Class\n\nYou don’t need to be an artist to enjoy making beautiful blue 
 cyanotypes! In this introductory class you’ll learn all the basics of th
 is fun and easy alternative photographic technique. Using light sensitive 
 chemicals you’ll expose prints of plants in the sun and process them in 
 water. By the time you leave you’ll have four gorgeous 8 x 10 blueprints
  and the know-how to create more at home. Lots of beautiful plants are bud
 ding and blooming during each season of the year. Let’s celebrate the na
 tural world by making botanical blueprints together! La maestra habla espa
 ñol.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/botanical-blueprints-introd
 uction-to-cyanotype/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Sunset Series at Chappellet Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T203000
UID:260607CDIQZXxa40y_gMoOnEBujA
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate summer on the Meadow with Chappellet’s Summer Suns
 et Series. A relaxed\, all-inclusive evening of Chappellet wines\, wood-fi
 red pizza\, and live music\, set against the backdrop of breathtaking view
 s from Pritchard Hill.\n\nThis limited summer experience takes place on th
 e last Saturday in June\, July\, and August\, and includes:\n\n·    
      A curated picnic pack with dining essentials (Go Vinos\, composta
 ble plates\, and cutlery)\n\n·         Caesar Salad\, Artisanal W
 ood-Fired Pizza\, & Chappellet Chardonnay Brittle\n\n·         Va
 let parking\n\n·         Chappellet wine by the glass—Chardonna
 y\, Pinot Noir\, Signature Cabernet Sauvignon\n\n·         Exclus
 ive savings on pre-selected bottles & merchandise to be enjoyed with your 
 picnic (inquire after reserving your ticket)\n\nGuests are encouraged to b
 ring picnic blankets or lawn chairs. Limited communal table seating is ava
 ilable on a first-come\, first-served basis.
LOCATION:Chappellet Winery
URL:https://chappellet.com/summer-sunset-series/ 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:H&L Live: Dan Martin & The Noma Rocksteady Band
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T153000
UID:260606hP4WmPHh3Ua35h5c9kbdbg
DESCRIPTION:**H&L Live: Dan Martin & the Noma Rocksteady Band**\n\nSpend a
  summer afternoon among the vines with the infectious sounds of Dan Martin
  & the Noma Rocksteady Band. Hailing from Sonoma\, these North Bay favorit
 es bring old-school Rocksteady\, Reggae\, and Ska inspired by the classic 
 Jamaican sounds of the 1960s and early '70s. Voted Best Reggae Band in the
  North Bay by readers of the North Bay Bohemian\, Dan Martin and his 7-pie
 ce band are guaranteed to move your feet and lift your spirits.\n\nThis is
  what our stage was built for: great artists\, beautiful afternoons\, and 
 the Russian River Valley as your backdrop. Bring a blanket\, grab a glass\
 , and settle in for one of those perfect wine country moments.\n\n**What t
 o Know:**\n\n**Admission is free** - just show up and enjoy\n\n**Pizza & C
 hill Red:** Fresh wood-fired pizza paired with our new Chill Red\n\n**Outd
 oor seating** - Lawn and picnic area available (bring blankets encouraged)
 \n\n**All ages welcome** - Family-friendly event\n\n**Wine available** for
  purchase by the glass or bottle\n\nCome for the music\, stay for the pizz
 a\, and remember why Saturdays in Sonoma County are the best.\n\n**Learn m
 ore about the band:** nomarocksteady.com\n\n‍\n\n‍
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/hl-live-dan-martin-noma-rock
 steady-band
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Talks - School Days
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T113000
UID:2606061zAhCOWQf0KeWDCJ424gjg
DESCRIPTION:**Teachers\, Text Books and School Spirit**\n\nSteve Deas\n\nS
 chools have long been institutions of key importance in Healdsburg. Steve 
 Deas will look at the early days of education\, when farm kids got their b
 asic education in one-room country school houses and the Seventh Day Adven
 tist community established a college that sat near the center of town. The
 n he’ll talk about more modern schools and their importance in the commu
 nity. And we’ll ask the audience to share stories of favorite teachers\,
  classroom hijinks and school Spirit.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
