BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Broadway Under the Stars - Ain't Too Proud: The Life and Times of 
 the Temptations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T000000
UID:2606117J23AMv-2kGqpRiUxAyAgQ
DESCRIPTION:Ain't Too Proud is the Tony-winning\, electrifying musical tha
 t follows The Temptations' extraordinary journey from the streets of Detro
 it to the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame. Featuring their signature dance moves 
 and unforgettable harmonies\, this musical takes audiences behind the musi
 c: how the group formed\, the unprecedented chart-topping success they ach
 ieved \\(42 Top Ten hits\, 14 \\#1 singles\\)\, and the personal and polit
 ical tensions that threatened their unity during a turbulent era in Americ
 a. This thrilling story of brotherhood\, family loyalty and betrayal is se
 t to the beat of the group's treasured hits\, including "My Girl\," "Just 
 My Imagination\," "Get Ready\," "Papa Was a Rolling Stone" and so many mor
 e\, with a book by award-winning playwright Dominique Morisseau \\(Skeleto
 n Crew\, Paradise Blue\\) adapted from Williams's 1988 memoir. The New Yor
 k Times praised the show as\, "Pretty close to perfect"\, with The Washing
 ton Post proclaiming it was "Dazzling and Electrifying." Ain't Too Proud i
 s presented through special arrangement with Music Theatre International \
 \(MTI\\). All authorized performance materials are also supplied by MTI. w
 ww.mtishows.com Music Theatre International gives Ain't Too Proud: The Lif
 e and Times of the Temptations a PG13 rating. This production is a gritty\
 , authentic look at the history of The Temptations. Parental discretion is
  advised.
LOCATION:Sonoma Field of Dreams
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
