BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Brandlin Estate Wine & Food Tasting Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T160000
UID:260312gwObQGIY00W9QT4IuHcTEw
DESCRIPTION:Born on the rugged slopes of Mount Veeder\, Brandlin Estate pr
 oduces wines of structure\, intensity\, and place. The Brandlin Experience
  offers an in-depth exploration of this historic vineyard site through a c
 urated tasting of five estate-grown wines—including Zinfandel from centu
 ry-old vines and the estate’s signature Cabernet Sauvignon. This seated\
 , guided experience invites guests to delve into the mountain terroir thro
 ugh the lens of small-lot winemaking. Each wine reflects the elevation\, e
 xposure\, and rocky soils that define the Brandlin Estate. For an added di
 mension\, guests may opt to include seasonal bites\, thoughtfully paired t
 o complement the structure and complexity of the wines. This experience is
  hosted at the picturesque Boathouse.
LOCATION:Brandlin Estate 
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/brandlinestate/experience/565565/the-brand
 lin-wine-food-tasting-experience?date=2026-03-12&size=2&time=10%3A00
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Greg Lamboy Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T000000
UID:260312-Dl23Gwo_EuOSSMuoXOscg
DESCRIPTION:Greg Lamboy is a Northern California singer-songwriter whose p
 erformances combine lyrical honesty\, melodic craft\, and soulful acoustic
  guitar. Known for his confident yet comforting stage presence\, Greg weav
 es together original songs and reimagined favorites that invite listeners 
 to slow down and connect. His music blends strength and sensitivity\, reve
 aling deep emotion without pretense and reminding audiences why live music
  matters.
LOCATION:B.R. Cohn Winery
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107773055?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T094500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260627T101500
UID:260212r2CbOB5aVUCYedd1Om5djA
DESCRIPTION:**Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.**\n\nOvereater
 s Anonymous (OA) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits. \n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on first
 \, second and fourth **Saturdays of the month from 9:45 - 10:15 AM at** 
 ​**Unitarian Universalist Congregation of Marin\, 240 Channing Way\, San
  Rafael CA 94903**. Contact: Sue M. 415-298-6792​. You may view all Nor
 th Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northbayoa.org/meet
 ings.html\n\nIn OA\, members experience **spiritual\, emotional\, and phys
 ical recovery** by practicing the **Twelve Steps** and living by their spi
 ritual principles—one day at a time.\n\nOA is **not** a diet club or cal
 orie-counting program.\n\nMembers have different plans of eating.\n\nOA do
 es **not** endorse any specific food plan. \n\nIf food is causing problem
 s in your life\, you don’t have to struggle alone. Recovery is possible\
 , and help is available.\n\n**Visit:** https://www.northbayoa.org/\n\n**Fi
 nd a meeting:** https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Unitarian Universalist Congregation of Marin
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
