BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wendy The Welder & The Mare Island Shipyard Workers - JeanCherie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T160000
UID:260617eT1IzWUSHkevuImUnOFyMg
DESCRIPTION:Mare Island Art Studios is proud to present Wendy the Welder &
  The Mare Island Shipyard Workers\, a powerful new exhibition by artist Je
 anCherie and guest artists honoring the women who helped shape Mare Island
  history during World War II.\n\nAt the heart of the exhibit is Wendy the 
 Welder\, a sculpture inspired by the more than 11\,000 women who built shi
 ps on Mare Island during the war effort. The piece celebrates the strength
 \, resilience\, and lasting impact of these women whose contributions help
 ed shape both local and national history.\n\nJeanCherie\, a Vallejo artist
  and member of Mare Island Art Studios\, created the sculpture as a tribut
 e to the workers of her mother’s generation and the spirit of the Mare I
 sland community. Her vision is to help bring greater recognition to this i
 mportant history through the creation of a future large-scale public sculp
 ture for the Mare Island Core.
LOCATION:Mare Island Art Studios
URL:https://mareislandartstudios.com/events/wendy-the-welder-the-mare-isla
 nd-shipyard-workers-jeancherie/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
