BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Sundays Music Series at Montgomery Village
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T140000
UID:260618Gd1VtqSuzUiQ81AEzRZtog
DESCRIPTION:Summer Sundays Music Series at Montgomery Village\n\nFree live
  music\, good vibes\, and a great excuse to make a Sunday out of it.\n\nSu
 mmer Sundays Music Series is a free monthly event bringing live music to t
 he Courtyard at Montgomery Village all summer long. This year\, we’re fe
 aturing local saxophonist Jimmy Galvan\, whose sound sets the perfect back
 drop for a relaxed afternoon in the heart of Sonoma County. Come for the m
 usic\, stay for the shopping\, dining\, coffee and ice cream. No tickets\,
  no fuss\, just a great community afternoon.\n\nJoin us on Sunday\, June 2
 8th from 12–2pm in the Courtyard at Montgomery Village \\(located near M
 onti’s\, Salt & Straw and Anthropologie\\). We invite you to grab a bite
  or treat from your favorite Village restaurant or cafe\, then settle into
  the Courtyard and enjoy the sounds of summer. Summer Sundays are free and
  open to the community.\n\nCan’t make it in June? Future events are sche
 duled for Sunday\, July 19th and Sunday\, August 16th.
LOCATION:Montgomery Village
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/summer-sundays-music-series-2/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Show Reception: Conversations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260628T160000
UID:260617jlwNe_I86kGFFZcdo0gB_A
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Sebastopol Regional Library from 2-4pm and meet the
  artists of Conversations: A Multimedia Exhibit of People Pictures\, a sim
 ultaneous showing of art by Sandra Rubin and Stephen French\, on display i
 n the library forum room May 26\, 2026 through July 18\, 2026. Enjoy refre
 shments\, conversation and art. Artists' Statements Sandra Rubin The paint
 ings I intend to include are mostly figures and portraits\, drawn and pain
 ted expressively\, energetically and intuitively\, with watercolor\, paste
 l and oil paints\, often combined with charcoal or graphite. I am excited 
 and honored to participate in this upcoming show\, Conversations: A Multim
 edia Exhibit of People Pictures\, with my friend and colleague Steve Frenc
 h. Stephen French I've been an artist for as long as I can remember. As a 
 kid\, I doodled on everything and made up my own cartoons. I loved comic b
 ooks and the Saturday matinees\, and Walt Disney movies really lit a spark
  in me. Watching the Disney TV show\, I was blown away to learn that peopl
 e actually drew all that animation. That curiosity led me to art school\, 
 where I studied fine art and art history. At the same time\, I developed a
  love for gardening. I earned a certificate in ornamental horticulture and
  worked as a gardener and later as a landscape contractor and landscape ar
 chitect. Those years designing gardens and outdoor spaces gave me somethin
 g important: a deep interest in how people connect with their surroundings
 . Eventually\, that idea brought me full circle back to painting and drawi
 ng. I realized what fascinates me most is people just being themselves in 
 the environments they live in. That's where I find endless inspiration. I'
 ve worked in oils\, acrylics\, and even experimented with acrylic on Tyvek
 . Lately\, I've been enjoying drawing on my iPad\, too. Whatever the mediu
 m\, I'm always chasing that same thing I noticed as a kid-people and the w
 orlds they create around them.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Regional Library
URL:https://events.sonomalibrary.org/event/art-show-reception-sandy-steve-
 95448
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
