BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TAKE YOUR TIME: Oil Pintings by Sharon Eisley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T170000
UID:260529oKbyH4Nr0kmNsMpAYgPEZg
DESCRIPTION:“Take Your Time”\n\nChange and transformation take time. I
 n her newest oil paintings Sharon Eisley explores the time as a process. B
 e it moving through grief\, re-framing your story of self\, or birthing so
 me new creation\, each painting lures you in with beautiful application th
 en holds you in time for a closer examination of our human experience. Eis
 ley's paintings are all inspired by tarot cards and her personal journey. 
 Tarot readings will be offered at the reception by @SymbolWarehouse for an
  optional small donation.\n\nOur guest artist\, Robert Benson\, will be ch
 allenging your eyes to fill in the details with his impressionist watercol
 ors.\n\nThis June 20th reception will be the FINAL art opening for Sebasto
 pol Gallery in its home of almost 20 years! This show may last only throug
 h June 2026\, then move to our new location. Or it may be up through June 
 and July. Either way\, this will be your last chance to come celebrate our
  local\, amazing group of artists at 150 N Main St.. “Take Your Time” 
 is a reminder to our collective to take our time finding and setting up ou
 r new home for all of you. I hope you can all come celebrate all the time 
 and art we shared with you in our lovely gallery.\n\nwww.sharoneisley.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Little Shop of Horrors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T163000
UID:260528eu34k8Pq4EKeMe6XZ2lC-w
DESCRIPTION:Howard Ashman and Alan Menken gave the world this camp classic
  in 1982. They based musical \\(loosely\\) on the low-budget 1960 black co
 medy film The Little Shop of Horrors\, with Menken’s score featuring sp
 ectacular music: early 1960s-style rock and roll\, doo-wop\, and early Mot
 own.\n\nThe story centers on meek floral assistant Seymour Krelborn\, who 
 stumbles across a new breed of plant he names “Audrey II” after his co
 worker crush. This foul-mouthed\, R&B-singing carnivore promises unending 
 fame and fortune to the down-and-out Krelborn as long as he keeps feeding 
 it BLOOD. Over time\, though\, Seymour discovers Audrey II’s out-of-this
 -world origins and its intent toward global domination!\n\nJune 26\, 27\, 
 28\; July 2\\*\, 3\, 5\, 9\, 10\, 11\, 12\n\nFriday and Saturday Shows: 7:
 30 PM\n\nSunday Matinee: 2:00 PM\n\n\\*Value Thursday: 7:30 PM\n\nBook and
  Lyrics by Howard Ashman\n\nMusic By Alan Menken  \n\nDirector     
              Katie Watts-Whitaker\n\nMusic Director      
   Kelly Considine\n\nChoreographer       Katie Watts-Whitaker
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/little-shop/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
