BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Penngrove Parade and BBQ
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T160000
UID:260519NcvbAYcDFEyPsf8BrfSNRw
DESCRIPTION:Stars\, Stripes\, and A Parade! Celebrate 250 Years at the Pen
 ngrove Parade's 50th Parade at 11 am\, and deep pit BBQ in the Park. Music
  by Train Wreck Junction.\n\nPenngrove Parade – 50th annual parade \n\n
 “The Biggest Little Parade in Northern California” Sunday\, July 5\, 2
 026 11 a.m. sharp - Parade on Downtown Penngrove on Main Street\n\nFree to
  Enter - entries due July 1\n\nNoon – 4 pm – BBQ and music by Train W
 reck Junction in Penngrove Park\, 11800 Main St.\, Penngrove 94951. \n\
 nTheme: \n\nStars\, Stripes\, and A Parade! \n\nCelebrate 50 & 250 Years a
 t the Penngrove Parade\n\nIt's as small-town America as you can get. You
 ’ll see tractors\, horses\, floats\, antique military Jeeps\, bands\, an
 d bicycle teams. And\, it's blissfully under one hour!\n\nThe menu offers
  old-fashioned pit beef\, BBQ chicken\, beef sandwiches\, oysters\, and ho
 t dogs. Drinks and Lagunitas beer will keep you cool. You’ll want to vis
 it the Penngrove 4-H dessert and cold soda booth. Purchase barbecue ticket
 s at the door.\n\n Grand Marshal Ray Soper will lead the parade in an his
 toric fire engine. Soper has been involved with Penngrove Social Firemen f
 or decades and is a past president. ​ Know Before You Go: Sorry\, no do
 gs\, coolers\, outside food or drink in the park. No digital ID will be ac
 cepted. Bring cash or use the on-site ATM.  ​ This is the biggest annua
 l fundraiser hosted by Penngrove Social Firemen\, a non-profit 501\\(c\\)
 \\(3\\)\, to benefit the Penngrove community.\n\nFunds help maintain the P
 enngrove Clubhouse and Penngrove Park\, and support local groups. Parade e
 ntry forms are available at Penngrove Market or online at  www.penngroves
 ocialfiremen.org. Entries must be received at Penngrove Market no later 
 than Wednesday\, July 1st\, by 8 PM\, or emailed to mrsjjava@hotmail.com
 .\n\nPhone \\(707\\) 318-2191\n\n Stay in touch at:\n\nhttps://www.penng
 rovesocialfiremen.org\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/groups/339347940599\n\nh
 ttps://www.instagram.com/penngrovesocialfiremen/\n\nJuly 5\, 2026 - Ranch
 o Adobe Firefighters Association will be presenting the pancake breakfast 
 on July 5 at 4h 2026 from 0700-1100. This event is free to the community 
 and donations are accepted. For information\, contact Morgan DeJong\, mde
 jong@rafd.org.
LOCATION:Penngrove Park
URL:https://www.penngrovesocialfiremen.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T170000
UID:260508EojcsOeLf0GC2nLesW15gA
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Sundays on the Plaza - Dirty Cello
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260705T170000
UID:260502P9R8uKXKQUuso5kd5DHnyw
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Music in Place and the City of Sonoma invite you
  to soak up the sunshine\, sip local wine\, and dance to live music at the
  Sonoma Plaza Grinstead Amphitheater during Sonoma Sundays On the Plaza\, 
 a free concert series running June 7 through October 4\, 2026.\n\nThis wee
 k's lineup features Dirty Cello! Cello like you’ve never heard before! C
 ombine the virtuosic wail of Jimi Hendrix\, the soul of BB King\, and the 
 fire of Bill Monroe\, and add a whole lot of cello\, and you get the Dirty
  Cello band. With wild vocals\, and world class cello playing\, the group 
 is led by vivacious cross-over cellist\, Rebecca Roudman.\n\nSonoma Sunday
 s are free and open to all\, thanks to the generous support of the Sonoma 
 Community Center\, The Dawn Redwoods Trust\, and the McNeely Family Founda
 tion.\n\nPack your picnic\, bring your dancing shoes\, and meet us on the 
 Plaza!
LOCATION:Grinstead Amphitheater
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/sonoma-sundays-on-the-plaza-7-5/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
