BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Common Ground Bookclub- Disability Pride Event
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260709T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260709T113000
UID:260525qDNKWbOvKkO4vNi7oVaM_w
DESCRIPTION:Common Ground Society and the Sonoma County Library are partne
 ring to create a Common Ground Book Club. Meet with others to discuss book
 s centering on disability voices. Each month we will read and discuss book
 s about and written by people with disabilities. In July we will be readin
 g Far From the Tree: Parents\, Children and the Search for Identity by Sol
 omon\, Andrew. If you don't have time to read or finish the book you are s
 till welcome to attend. Copies of the books are available through the Sono
 ma County Regional Libraries. Registration is encouraged but not required 
 - drop ins are welcome. Snacks will be provided. \\*\\*Most books are avai
 lable for free in the audio format through Libby\, and/or Hoopla \\(librar
 y card required\\) Accessibility: The parking lot is paved and has several
  accessible parking spots. There are ramps leading into the building from 
 the parking lot on the west side facing N. High St. The library is fully a
 ccessible inside.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Regional Library
URL:https://events.sonomalibrary.org/event/common-ground-bookclub-disabili
 ty-pride-event-109064
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
