BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Uytengsu Family Opening Night at Charles Krug
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260710T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260710T200000
UID:260613XS0KviiEM0y87Xjgp5IgoQ
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the grand opening of Festival Napa Valley's mileston
 e 20th Anniversary Season with a spectacular evening of music at the histo
 ric Charles Krug winery in St. Helena. Led by the dynamic conductor Stepha
 nie Childress\, this festive Opening Night program bridges centuries of mu
 sical tradition — from the power of Beethoven's Coriolan Overture to daz
 zling new works and beloved American standards reimagined for a full symph
 ony orchestra.    The evening features the world premiere of a new concert
 o by composer Michael Thurber\, commissioned by Festival Napa Valley and w
 ritten expressly for the Grammy Award-winning ensemble Time for Three. Als
 o on the program is Young America\, a stirring six-movement cycle for chor
 us and orchestra by acclaimed composer Gordon Getty\, brought to life by t
 he Young People's Chorus of New York City under the artistic direction of 
 Francisco J. Nuñez. The night culminates in a thrilling symphonic reimagi
 ning of iconic songs by Bob Dylan\, Billy Joel\, and other American legend
 s.    This choose-your-own-price event \\(starting at $5\, with a $35 sugg
 ested donation\\). It's the perfect way to kick off a summer of extraordin
 ary arts and wine country experiences.
LOCATION:Charles Krug Winery
URL:https://www.winecountry.com/event/uytengsu-family-opening-night-from-b
 eethoven-to-getty-to-dylan-at-charles-krug/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
